WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.950
Tin is a metal, and like other
metals, it conducts electricity.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.610
Combine tin with chlorine and you
get tin four chloride, a liquid.

3
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.230
Dip two electrodes into the
liquid, and nothing flows.

4
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.070
Not even a flicker.

5
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.530
Tin conducts.

6
00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:20.310
So why doesn't liquid tin
four chloride conduct at all?

7
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.930
In this mission, you'll
explore the metallic bond,

8
00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.230
and explain why metals conduct,
bend and melt the way they do.

9
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.530
You'll see why alloys are harder,

10
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:34.810
and place any binary compound on the
bonding triangle to predict its properties.

11
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:40.050
Your mission: explain why liquid tin four
chloride doesn't conduct electricity.
